# The negation of a 2-limb number, limb by limb: exact, and still normalized.
kernel:        neg_2
input:         x = x0 x1
output:        z = z0 z1
value:         -x
requires:      canonical x
ensures:       normalized z
ensures:       error z R c=0 k=2 t=0
ensures:       represents z
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/Sign.v neg_2_correct
source:        limb by limb (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   z1 = -x1 does not reach z0; a negation is exact and cannot overflow, and a non-finite x1 beside a finite x0 is not a normalized operand, so the non-finite layer, which reads x0, stands in for the check

z0 = neg(x0)
z1 = neg(x1)
